Z||000000||Gold87SE||04-28-2001||10:02 AM||||hi <P>I'm locked out of my fiero which has a sunroof. I remember hearing that there's a way to get in through the sun roof but I forget how.||||reg||1
Z||000001||KRMFiero||04-28-2001||10:21 AM||||This has been covered a bunch of times, do a search....    I think with the sunroof (Im not sure, i dont have one) if you punch next to it a sertin way it will pop open, worth a shot.....   ||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||04-28-2001||01:41 PM||||easiest thing is for $1.00 get a spare door key. hide it on the car somewhere or keep in your wallet.||||reg||1
Z||000003||JetroGT||04-28-2001||03:43 PM||||I just take a screwdriver and pull the glass far enough out to get my fingertips in. Then I pull the glass out further to put my arm in, then it's unlocked. It works best if you have skinny arms. If you pull it out too far you risk breaking the glass. Ouch! I've done this many times on my cars, power widndows and manual with no ill effects to the car.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Spektyr||04-28-2001||05:50 PM||||Yup, this was a common theft tactic used on the early 90's Talons/Eclipses.<P>Right next to the bottom of the radiator on one side is the siren wire for the factory alarm.  Cut that, no siren.  Then pry top of window glass out with screwdriver, have a skinny-armed guy reach down inside and unlock the car.  The lights flash, but that's it.  This was a big target for the stereo-thieves.<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gold87SE||04-29-2001||12:55 AM||||I was able to get in with the screwdriver technique. Thanks for the help.||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||04-29-2001||06:21 AM||||get that extra key yet?||||reg||7
Z||000007||Spektyr||05-14-2001||01:18 PM||||LOL, well my dumb self just locked the keys in the car.  And since I'd never do something that dumb, I hadn't had a second set of keys made yet.<P>Hurts a bit to jam your arm down inside the window, but I got it open.<P>A little annoying how easy that is...<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||1
